# Paths whose pull requests need a review before the merge queue lands them
# (#6173). Every other pull request lands on its own green checks and the
# batch's merged-tree verification, with no review.
#
# One glob per line, under a [boundary] heading. `*` stays within one path
# component, `**/x` matches x in any directory, and `x/**` everything under
# x. A line starting `**/` names a file by its name, so it matches in any
# case (AUTH-POLICY.md, OAuth); every other line is case-sensitive. Only `*`
# and `**` are used, so the queue's matcher and the repository check agree.
#
# The queue reads this file from main, never from the pull request, and a
# missing, empty or unreadable list makes every path a boundary. A rename
# counts at both its paths, and a symlink, a submodule or a mode change is a
# boundary wherever it is. Tests are not exempt: a test that pins a boundary
# rule is part of it. This file is itself a boundary (ci-trust). Each line
# keeps a real example in merge-queue-boundary-examples, and
# `scripts/checks/repo_checks.py merge-queue-boundary` checks both.
